{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1082", "sample_idx": 39, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e4b-it", "content": "Arthur blinked, the morning sun surprisingly vibrant. He stretched, a familiar ache in his shoulders, but something felt…off. The colors were too saturated, the birdsong too melodic, the dew on the grass shimmered with an unnatural luminescence. He looked around his bedroom, a perfectly rendered space he vaguely recognized, yet felt detached from. A notification popped into his vision, a translucent box hovering near his temple: \"Welcome, Arthur! You have entered Aethelgard - Realm of Valor. Level 1 achieved.\" Panic seized him. He tried to grab his phone, but his hand passed right through it. He looked at his reflection in the mirror, noticing details he'd never observed before - subtle glowing lines tracing his musculature, a faint HUD overlaying his vision displaying health and stamina bars. He was in a video game.\n\n***\n\nHe cautiously ventured outside, the world unfolding in breathtaking detail. Lush forests stretched as far as the eye could see, crystalline rivers snaked through valleys, and distant mountains pierced the sky. A small, wooden signpost appeared before him, displaying options: \"Quest: Retrieve the Sunstone.\" \"Explore the Whispering Woods.\" \"Speak with Elder Rowan.\" Arthur felt a strange mix of terror and exhilaration. He tentatively clicked on \"Quest: Retrieve the Sunstone,\" and a detailed objective appeared: \"Find the Sunstone within the Goblin Caves. Defeat the Goblin King.\" A wave of nausea washed over him. This wasn't a dream; this was real, terrifyingly real. He took a deep breath, the air smelling of pine and something else…something digital. He had a quest. He had to survive.\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "Arthur", "logprob": -0.18361379206180573}, {"token": "▁blinked", "logprob": -0.32705190777778625}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.0002044230350293219}, {"token": "▁the", "logprob": -0.10078337788581848}, {"token": "▁mo